  "name": "Q'ero song and pinkuyllu (Paucartambo high puna)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "The Q'ero communities of the high puna of Paucartambo in Cusco keep a repertoire of songs addressed to their llamas and alpacas and to the mountain beings, sung chiefly by women in a high voice, while men play the pinkuyllu, a long duct flute, at Carnival. John Cohen's Folkways recordings and Holly Wissler's later fieldwork document this repertoire. The flute card stands in for the pinkuyllu.",
